  "notes": "Tailwind slate dark theme (slate-950 page, slate-900 header/sidebar, slate-800 reply cards) with blue-500 user bubbles. Cartoon cat avatars mark the bot and a raccoon/cat marks the user, a playful touch on an otherwise utilitarian UI. Each reply opens with a Hide/Show thinking toggle that reveals a monospace reasoning block, separated from the answer by a white rule. Code blocks have a language label ('TSX') and a Copy button on a darker header strip, plus One Dark highlighting; long lines get cut off rather than wrapped. The composer has kbd-style chips for shortcuts (send, newline, Tab complete, history). The send button is disabled and invisible while the input is empty. The thread is centred at about 860px max width. The theme toggle sits in the header."
